ay} \\right. \\end{displaymath} which partially answered an open problem of Wang on Davenport constant for the multiplicative semigroup of $\\frac{\\F_q[x]}{(f)}$ (G.Q. Wang, \\emph{Davenport constant for semigroups II,} Journal of Number Theory, 155 (2015) 124--134).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLower bounds for the energy of graphs (https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1016/j.akcej.2017.10.007)\nciteturn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.4 years ago; Crawled: last week; If $G$ is a graph with $n$ vertices, $m$ edges, and $minimum\\phantom{\\rule{0.33em}{0ex}}degree$ $\\delta $. ... ## 3 Lower bounds for the energy of graphs\n\nIn this section we present lower bounds for $\\mathcal{E}\\left(G\\right)$ in terms of number of vertices, edges, Randić index, minimum degree, diameter, walk and determinant of the adjacency matrix.\n\nIf $G$ is a $connected$ graph with $n$ vertices and diameter $D$. Then (8) ${\\lambda }_{1}\\ge \\sqrt[D]{n-1}.$(8)\n\nLemma 6\n\n## [Citation19]\n\nIf $G$ is a graph with $n$ vertices, $m$ edges, and $minimum\\phantom{\\rule{0.33em}{0ex}}degree$ $\\delta $. Then (9) ${\\lambda }_{1}⩾\\frac{2(m-\\delta )}{n-1}.$(9)\n\nLemma 7\n\n## [Citation20]\n\nLet $G$ be a connected graph and $k⩾0$. Then (10) ${\\lambda }_{1}⩾\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum _{v\\in V}{d}_{k+1\\left(v\\right)}^{2}}{\\sum _{v\\in V}{d}_{k\\left(v\\right)}^{2}}}.$(10)\n\n## 3 Lower bounds for the energy of graphs\n\nIn this section we present lower bounds for $\\mathcal{E}\\left(G\\right)$ in terms of number of vertices, edges, Randić index, minimum degree, diameter, walk and determinant of the adjacency matrix.\n\nTheorem 1\n\nLet $G$ be a non-empty and non-singular graph with $n$ vertices, $m$ edges. Then (11) $\\mathcal{E}\\left(G\\right)⩾\\frac{m}{R}+(n-1)+ln\\mid detA\\mid -ln\\left(\\frac{m}{R}\\right).$(11) Equality holds if and only if $G\\cong {K}_{n}$.\n\nProof\n\nSince $G$ is non-singular, it is $\\mid {\\lambda 